remarks.format:
## Remarks

An <xref:SkiaSharp.SKGraphiteContext> owns the connection to a GPU backend (Dawn, Metal, or Vulkan) and is used to create recorders, insert recordings, and submit recorded work to the GPU. Create a context with one of the backend-specific factory methods, such as <xref:SkiaSharp.SKGraphiteContext.CreateMetal%2A>, <xref:SkiaSharp.SKGraphiteContext.CreateVulkan%2A>, or <xref:SkiaSharp.SKGraphiteContext.CreateDawn%2A>.

The context is disposable and owns unmanaged GPU resources, so it should be disposed when it is no longer needed, typically with a `using` statement.

## Examples

The following example creates a Metal-backed context, records some drawing, and submits it to the GPU:

```csharp
var backendContext = new SKGraphiteMtlBackendContext
{
    MtlDevice = mtlDevice,
    MtlQueue = mtlQueue,
};

using var context = SKGraphiteContext.CreateMetal(backendContext);
using var recorder = context.CreateRecorder(0);

var info = new SKImageInfo(256, 256);
using (var surface = SKSurface.Create(recorder, info))
{
    var canvas = surface.Canvas;
    canvas.Clear(SKColors.CornflowerBlue);
}

using var recording = recorder.Snap();
context.InsertRecording(recording);
context.Submit();
```
